WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.953
Nvidia Is Powering

00:00:01.765 --> 00:00:03.475
Brain-Computer Interfaces

00:00:03.286 --> 00:00:03.887
Now

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:05.707
Nvidia is now

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:06.992
powering brain-computer

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:07.806
interfaces

00:00:07.913 --> 00:00:08.985
bringing its chips

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:09.976
to neural implants

00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:11.131
that translate brain

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.334
signals into action

00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:14.359
The Paradromics implant

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:15.137
uses more than

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:16.800
400 embedded electrodes

00:00:16.624 --> 00:00:17.531
to capture those

00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:18.038
signals

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.123
and a computer

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:20.833
uses artificial intelligence

00:00:20.739 --> 00:00:21.812
to make inferences

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:22.508
about what she’s

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.262
trying to say

00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:25.036
Making brain-computer

00:00:24.848 --> 00:00:26.368
interfaces practical

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.194
and portable for

00:00:27.006 --> 00:00:28.043
patients is a

00:00:27.855 --> 00:00:29.081
major challenge for

00:00:28.892 --> 00:00:29.658
the field

00:00:29.798 --> 00:00:31.189
Made by brain-computer

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.981
interface company Paradromics

00:00:33.111 --> 00:00:34.243
the implant is

00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:35.339
outwardly invisible

00:00:35.411 --> 00:00:36.365
but the speech

00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:37.415
decoding requires a

00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:38.146
cart full of

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:38.948
electronics

00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:40.500
Full story on

00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:41.207
the dashboard
